  BEFORE: against 19.79 Bcf/d, a year before (31 Oct 2025)
  AFTER:  against 19.79 Bcf/d, a year before (31 Oct 2025). California's part of this total is EIA-930's hours before 16 December 2025 and CAISO's own supply by fuel from that day, so this comparison crosses a change of source. EIA's California natural gas ran about 30 percent above CAISO's own in 2024 and about 47 percent above it in 2025 (the weeks both hold), so the change against those years is lower than the gas burned alone would make it.
